    <statement><p>Find the equation of the plane which passes through <m>O</m> and is parallel to <m>x+6y+z=-4</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0001"/><m>x+</m> <fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0002"/><m>y+z=</m><fillin characters="1" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\bf{n}</m><m>=\left\lt 1,6,1\right&gt;</m> is normal to the plane <m>x+6y+z=-4</m>, and so is also normal to the parallel plane. Setting <m>\bf{n}</m><m>=\left\lt 1,6,1\right&gt;</m> and <m>\left( x_0,y_0,x_0\right)=\left(0,0,0\right)</m> in the vector equation of the plane yields 



<m>\left\lt 1,6,1\right&gt; \cdot \left\lt x,y,z\right&gt; =\left\lt 1,6,1\right&gt; \cdot \left\lt 0,0,0\right&gt;=0</m> 



<m>x+6y+z=0</m>






</solution>
